</Tags>
<Routines>
<Routine Name="aaReadMe" Type="ST">
<STContent>
<Line Number="0">
<![CDATA[/*]]>
</Line>
<Line Number="1">
<![CDATA[This routine describes how to run the sample project.]]>
</Line>
<Line Number="2">
<![CDATA[This project is also an example of superimposed motion.]]>
</Line>
<Line Number="3">
<![CDATA[]]>
</Line>
<Line Number="4">
<![CDATA[Step1 - Home all the Axis to 0 degree position. See in routine “PickPlace_with_Multiple_Tools”. Initialize gearing between Conveyor axis and Cartesian X axis of Robot’s base frame ]]>
</Line>
<Line Number="5">
<![CDATA[Step2 - Setup MCTO with Cart_XYZRxRyRz as Cartesian System, Delta 4 axis as Robot System. Toggle “Start_MCTO” tag to initiate MCTO. ]]>
</Line>
<Line Number="6">
<![CDATA[Step3 - Set different Tool frames using Tool Frame offsets values. See offset values in “Tool_Frame[]”array. ]]>
</Line>
<Line Number="7">
<![CDATA[Step4 - Toggle “Start_Conveyor” and move the conveyor axis thought MAJ. The MAG gears the conveyor_axis to X axis ]]>
</Line>
<Line Number="8">
<![CDATA[Step5 - Check "ToolChangeAllowedStatus" status and initiate new MCTO with new Tool Frame Offset values. Program object’s end position in MCPM.  ]]>
</Line>
<Line Number="9">
<![CDATA[		Check MCPM end position values in “Path_Position[]” data. Toggle “Start_Pick_n_Place” to start MCPMmove.]]>
</Line>
<Line Number="10">
<![CDATA[		The Path_Positions in MCPM are superimposed with X axis position in MAG]]>
</Line>
<Line Number="11">
<![CDATA[]]>
</Line>
<Line Number="12">
<![CDATA[Step6 - "Robot_EOA_Positions" routine computes Robot's End of Arm(EOA) positions from Base frame using MCTPO. ]]>
</Line>
<Line Number="13">
<![CDATA[Step7 - Run Trends. See TCP and End of Arm (EOA) XYZ position during the move. ]]>
</Line>
<Line Number="14">
<![CDATA[]]>
</Line>
<Line Number="15">
<![CDATA[]]>
</Line>
<Line Number="16">
<![CDATA[*/]]>
</Line>
</STContent>
</Routine>
<Routine Name="MainRoutine" Type="RLL">
<RLLContent>
<Rung Number="0" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[
All information provided  - No Warranty or implied merchantability. 
Refer to the RSLogix 5000 End User License Agreement (EULA) in the Release Notes.
]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[NOP();]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="1" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[=================================================================

Sample program for new Kinematics feature of Tool Frame Offsets, via MCTO programming;
MCTO is programed with three-finger gripper tool using different Tool Frame offset values.
 Robot is tracking the Conveyor and picking different objects from the conveyor by dynamically changing the Tool Frames on the fly.  
Target positions are programmed using path positions in the MCPM instruction. 


=====  MCTO Set up  =====
Cartesian system = CS_XYZRxRyRz (6 Virtual axes, Geometry=Cartesian, Definition = XYZRxRyRz)
Robot coordinate system = Delta_4_Axis (4 Joint axes, Geometry=Delta 3D, Definition = J1J2J3J6)  
Tool Frame [3] = Three different offset frames are used  


================================================================
Open Trend = to view the plot of robot’s TCP Positions 
	XY Plot shows object positions on the conveyor at TCP and End of Arm(EOA)
XZ Plot shows TCP moves during different pick cycles 
==================================================================
]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[[JSR(PickPlace_with_Multiple_Tools,0) ,JSR(Robot_EOA_Positions,0) ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="2" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[==========================
USER SETUP:::
Toggle bits from left to right.
===========================
Start_MCTO: Enables the Transformation between the Cartesian axes and Robot axes
Start_Conveyor: Moves to the Conveyor axis 
Start_Pick_n_Place: Does a PICK and PLACE with different Tool Frames 
]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIC(Start_MCTO)XIC(Start_Conveyor)XIC(Start_Pick_n_Place)OTU(unlatch);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="3" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[==================================================================
Conclusion 
With Tool Frame offsets multi finger grippers can be programmed to pick multiple objects by changing Tools dynamically, 

==========================
]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIC(MCSCart)XIC(MCSRobot)OTU(Stop_Program);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
</RLLContent>
</Routine>
<Routine Name="PickPlace_with_Multiple_Tools" Type="RLL">
<RLLContent>
<Rung Number="0" Type="N">
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIC(s:fs)MOV(0,Tool_Index)MOV(1,step);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="1" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[Home all the axis to 0-degree position.
Set up gearing between Conveyor and  Cartesian axis]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIC(MotionGroup.GroupSynced)EQU(step,1)MAH(J1,Mah_Ctr[0])MAH(J2,Mah_Ctr[1])MAH(J3,Mah_Ctr[2])MAH(J4,Mah_Ctr[3])XIC(Mah_Ctr[0].DN)XIC(Mah_Ctr[1].DN)XIC(Mah_Ctr[2].DN)XIC(Mah_Ctr[3].DN)MAG(X,Conveyor_Axis,MAG_ctr,0,1,1,1,Command,Real,Disabled,100,Units per sec2)MOV(2,step);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="2" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[Setup MCTO with Cart_XYZRxRyRz as Cartesian System, Delta 4 axis as Robot System 
Set different Tool frames using Tool Frame offsets array. 
Initiate MCTO with enabling “Start_MCTO” tag
]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIC(MotionGroup.GroupSynced)XIC(Start_MCTO)EQU(step,2)[MCTO(CS_XYZRxRyRz,Delta_4_Axis,Mcto_Ctr1,Work_Frame,Tool_Frame[0]) ,XIC(Mcto_Ctr1.IP) MOV(3,step) ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="3" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[Start Conveyor axis
Robot will track the Conveyor along the X axis]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[EQU(step,3)XIC(Start_Conveyor)MAJ(Conveyor_Axis,Maj_Ctr,0,1,Units per sec,50,Units per sec2,50,Units per sec2,Trapezoidal,50,50,Units per sec3,Disabled,Programmed,0,0)XIC(Maj_Ctr.IP)MOV(4,step);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="4" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[Check "ToolChangeAllowedStatus" status and initiate new MCTO with new Tool Frame Offset values.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[EQU(step,4)XIC(Start_Pick_n_Place)XIC(CS_XYZRxRyRz.ToolChangeAllowedStatus)[MCTO(CS_XYZRxRyRz,Delta_4_Axis,Mcto_Ctr[Tool_Index],Work_Frame,Tool_Frame[Tool_Index]) ,XIC(Mcto_Ctr[Tool_Index].IP) MOV(5,step) ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="5" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[============Start Path Moves ================
Pick the Object with Different Tools 
The X axis position in path data is superimposed with X axis positon from MAG 
 when the Conveyor_axis is moved by MAJ instruction on Rung 3]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[EQU(step,5)[MCPM(CS_XYZRxRyRz,mcpm_ctr[Tool_Index],Path_Position[Tool_Index],1,dynamic_data,0,None) ,XIC(mcpm_ctr[Tool_Index].IP) XIO(CS_XYZRxRyRz.MovePendingQueueFullStatus) MOV(6,step) ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="6" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[Move to Safe position +Z from the convryor]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[EQU(step,6)[MCPM(CS_XYZRxRyRz,mcpm_ctr_1,Path_Safe_Pos,1,dynamic_data,0,None) ,XIC(mcpm_ctr_1.IP) XIO(CS_XYZRxRyRz.MovePendingQueueFullStatus) MOV(7,step) ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="7" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[Update Tool Frame offsets and initiate new MCTO with new Tool Frame. 
Run the same program with updated Tool Frames 

]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[EQU(step,7)XIC(CS_XYZRxRyRz.ToolChangeAllowedStatus)[CLR(mcpm_ctr[Tool_Index].FLAGS) ,CLR(Mcto_Ctr[Tool_Index].FLAGS) ,CLR(mcpm_ctr_1.FLAGS) ]ADD(1,Tool_Index,Tool_Index)[LES(Tool_Index,3) MOV(3,step) ,GEQ(Tool_Index,3) MOV(8,step) ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="8" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[Move to End position]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[EQU(step,8)[MCPM(CS_XYZRxRyRz,mcpm_ctr_2,Path_End_Pso,1,dynamic_data,0,None) ,XIC(mcpm_ctr_2.PC) XIO(CS_XYZRxRyRz.MovePendingQueueFullStatus) MOV(9,step) ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="9" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[Stop Conveyor]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[EQU(step,9)XIC(mcpm_ctr_2.PC)MAS(Conveyor_Axis,MAS_Ctr,All,No,100,Units per sec2,No,100,Units per sec3)MOV(99,step);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="10" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[Stop Cartesian  Coordinate system ]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIC(MCSCart)MCS(CS_XYZRxRyRz,mcs_ctr[0],Coordinated Transform,0,0,0,0,0,0);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="11" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[Stop Robot Coordinate system 
]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIC(MCSRobot)MCS(Delta_4_Axis,mcs_ctr[1],Coordinated Transform,0,0,0,0,0,0);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
</RLLContent>
</Routine>
<Routine Name="Robot_EOA_Positions" Type="RLL">
<RLLContent>
<Rung Number="0" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[Verify Robot’s TCP positions from the Robot’s Base Frame to the End of Arm using the MCTPO Forward instruction with no Tool Frame offsets.  
" TCP_XY_no_ToolFrames_Plot "  shows robot’s TCP positions from the Robot's Base Frame during the MCPM moves. 
]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIC(Start_MCTO)MOV(Delta_4_Axis.ActualPosition[0],MCTPO_Input[0])MOV(Delta_4_Axis.ActualPosition[1],MCTPO_Input[1])MOV(Delta_4_Axis.ActualPosition[2],MCTPO_Input[2])MOV(Delta_4_Axis.ActualPosition[3],MCTPO_Input[4])MOV(Delta_4_Axis.ActualPosition[4],MCTPO_Input[4])MOV(Delta_4_Axis.ActualPosition[5],MCTPO_Input[5])CLR(mctpo_ctr.FLAGS)MCTPO(CS_XYZRxRyRz,Delta_4_Axis,mctpo_ctr,0,0,Forward,MCTPO_Input[0],MCTPO_Output,Robot_Config,Turns_Counter[0]);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
</RLLContent>
</Routine>
</Routines>
</Program>
</Programs>
